# Route I `CapSourceData`: the ACTUAL source `capSource : CapSource` of the certified 198-cap run

Data pinned (sha256) from the generator outputs read by pc29 `route_i_tangent_real.py`
(`RowField`, `ColumnField`) and `route_i_marked_cert.py` (`reference`, `row_field`):

* `decay2_route_i_tangent_trial_cube.npz`
  `bae5de6f65f9a8fe37686c9cec525acaee24bf6282437a7b0ef0ecd7236f3ed9`:
  `row_cells`/`row_mass` (gas), `col_cells`/`col_mass` (anchor 0 columns), `negative_aux`,
  `positive_aux` (16 x 94), `sigmas`, `radial_field`, `epsilon = 0.108`, `angles = 94`;
* `decay2_route_i_marked_trials.npz`
  `8300b0fc4a62248329c1e3327c98cc3d069f9e838c7ad173f7da8dd9fd4b153f`, column index 6
  (`alpha = 1/50`): the anchor-1 reference rows and columns.

The integer data are exactly those of pc29 `exact_rows` (cell ends `round(10^12 y)`, weights
`round(10^12 w)` for float weights `> 1e-9`, `a < b`) and `auxiliary` (entries `(i, j, round(10^12 w))`,
`w > 1e-9`). Weights are the exact rationals `p / sum p` (rows, columns; times `49/50` at anchor 1) and
`target * p / sum p` (auxiliary, `target = 1 - m_+` resp. `53/58 - m_-`), phases `pi j / 93`,
`sigma_i`, `radial_i` the decimal `repr (float)` values, `eps = 0.108 = 27/250` exactly (so
`q = exp (-27/500)`, the pinned `q = exp (-eps/2)` of pc29).

kcost: about 14k list entries, 4 `decide +kernel` sweeps of 704, 628, 706, 628 triples (about 6
Int comparisons each), 1671 auxiliary triples, 16 sigma entries; no multiplication of large
numbers: well under 100k kernel ops, expected below 10 K (1 K ~ 1 s kernel). All decided entries
are below `2^64` (distinct values do not collide in the low-64 Nat hash).
